  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Research and Innovation Systems for Africa (RISA) Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Research and Information Systems in Africa (RISA) Fund programme is a multi- country Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO)-funded project focusing supporting African research institutions. The intended impact of RISA is to create thriving national research and innovation systems in targeted countries that will contribute to economic growth and development. The RISA Fund brings together two FCDO Research and Evidence Division (RED) programmes that aim to support research and innovation systems in Africa: Strengthening Research Institutions in Africa (SRIA) and the African Technology and Innovation Partnership (ATIP).RISA seeks to strengthen research and innovation systems by developing a portfolio of well-designed, evidence-based projects in targeted African countries</narrative>
  </description>
